from tnx import *
def T(iy,iyn,*a): TA(10,iy,iyn,*a)
I3="Iyal 3: Culture (பண்பாடு)"
T(3,I3,"virunthu-potruthum","Virunthu Potruthum! (விருந்து போற்றுதும்!)",
 "A mother's snack for her child's friends is where Tamil hospitality begins.",
 "This prose lesson says that Tamil hospitality begins with the snack a mother gives to a friend who comes along with her son or daughter. In Tamil tradition, cooking mixed feeling with food, and a feast expressed culture.",
 "The lesson praises welcoming guests (விருந்தோம்பல்), a core Tamil value in literature from Thirukkural onwards.",
 "Terms: விருந்து (feast or guest), விருந்தோம்பல் (hospitality), பண்பாடு (culture) and உணவு (food).",
 ["விருந்து","விருந்தோம்பல்","பண்பாடு","உணவு","விருந்தினர்"],
 ("Hospitality is not a Tamil value.",["It is a core value.","It starts at home."]),
 ["m|விருந்தோம்பல் means|hospitality|trade|singing|Welcoming guests.","m|The lesson begins with|a mother's snack|a king's feast|a battle|A mother's snack.","t|Tamil culture values guests.|T|Yes.","m|விருந்தினர் means|guest|king|farmer|Guest.","s|What does உணவு mean?|food|Food.","t|Food carries feeling in Tamil tradition.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"kasikandam","Kasikandam (காசிக்காண்டம்) — a memorisation poem",
 "A Tamil poem in praise of the holy city of Kasi.",
 "Kasikandam is a Tamil poetic work, composed by Athiveerarama Pandiyan, that is based on the Sanskrit Kasi Khanda and describes the greatness of the city of Kasi. The textbook includes a poem to be memorised.",
 "The poem teaches the Tamil tradition of hospitality and charity through the verse selected here. Read its meaning in your textbook.",
 "Terms: காண்டம் (section or canto), காசி (Kasi) and மனப்பாடம். Learn the poem along with its meaning.",
 ["காசிக்காண்டம்","காண்டம்","காசி","புராணம்","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("Kasikandam is a prose lesson.",["It is a poem.","It must be memorised."]),
 ["m|Kasikandam is a|poem|play|map|A poetic work.","m|It praises the city of|Kasi|Madurai|Chennai|Kasi.","t|It is a memorisation poem.|T|Yes.","m|காண்டம் means|section|house|boat|Canto or section.","s|What is காசி?|a holy city;Kasi|Kasi.","t|It is based on a Sanskrit work.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"muthukumarasamy-pillaitamil","Muthukumarasamy Pillaitamil (முத்துக்குமாரசாமி பிள்ளைத்தமிழ்)",
 "Poets sang of a god or a hero as if he were a child.",
 "Pillaitamil is a minor literary form (சிற்றிலக்கியம்) in which a poet sings of a deity or hero as a child, with ten stages such as காப்பு, செங்கீரை, தால், சப்பாணி, முத்தம், வருகை, அம்புலி, சிற்றில், சிறுபறை and சிறுதேர். This poem is for Muthukumarasamy.",
 "The textbook poem shows the poet's love for the child-god. Read the poem for its meaning and its imagery.",
 "Terms: பிள்ளைத்தமிழ், சிற்றிலக்கியம், பருவம் (stage) and முத்தம் (kiss).",
 ["பிள்ளைத்தமிழ்","சிற்றிலக்கியம்","பருவம்","முத்தம்","காப்பு"],
 ("Pillaitamil is a travel book.",["It sings of a child.","It has ten stages."]),
 ["m|Pillaitamil is a|minor literary form|dictionary|novel|A sirrilakkiyam.","m|It sings of a god or hero as a|child|king|enemy|Child.","t|It has ten stages (paruvam).|T|Yes.","m|Which is a stage?|முத்தம்|போர்|பயணம்|Muththam.","s|பருவம் means|stage|Stage.","t|The first stage is காப்பு.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"koottanchoru-gopallapuram","Koottanchoru: Gopallapurathu Makkal (கூட்டாஞ்சோறு: கோபல்லபுரத்து மக்கள்) by Ki. Rajanarayanan",
 "Villagers welcome hungry strangers with simple food and open hearts.",
 "This is an extract from a novel by Ki. Rajanarayanan. It shows the hospitality of the simple, open-hearted villagers whose natural welcome and plain food make a traveller forget his tiredness. When guests arrive hungry, the villagers share what they have.",
 "The piece shows village life and community feeling, and teaches that hospitality does not depend on wealth.",
 "Terms: கூட்டாஞ்சோறு (food cooked together), கிராமம் (village), விருந்தோம்பல் and கி. ராஜநாராயணன்.",
 ["கூட்டாஞ்சோறு","கிராமம்","விருந்தோம்பல்","எளிமை","புதினம்"],
 ("The villagers refuse the guests.",["They welcome them.","They share their food."]),
 ["m|The author is|Ki. Rajanarayanan|Kannadasan|Kamban|Ki. Ra.","m|The villagers show|hospitality|anger|fear|They welcome guests.","t|The meal is simple.|T|Yes.","m|கிராமம் means|village|city|sea|Village.","s|What does எளிமை mean?|simplicity;simple|Simplicity.","t|The text is a novel extract.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"thogainilai-thodargal","Grammar: Thogainilaith thodargal (தொகைநிலைத் தொடர்கள்)",
 "In some phrases a word is silently dropped, yet the meaning is clear.",
 "தொகைநிலைத் தொடர் is a phrase where a connecting word or case ending is hidden (தொக்கு நிற்றல்). There are six kinds: வேற்றுமைத்தொகை, வினைத்தொகை, பண்புத்தொகை, உவமைத்தொகை, உம்மைத்தொகை and அன்மொழித்தொகை.",
 "For example, ஊறுகாய் ('pickle') hides nothing, but in ஊறுகாய் as a வினைத்தொகை the word 'ஊறிய' is hidden; in மலர்க்கை the simile 'மலர் போன்ற கை' is hidden. Practise opening such phrases out.",
 "To identify the type, first spell out the hidden word, then match it to the kind: case ending, verb, quality, simile, 'and' (உம்) or another meaning.",
 ["தொகைநிலைத்தொடர்","வினைத்தொகை","பண்புத்தொகை","உவமைத்தொகை","உம்மைத்தொகை"],
 ("There are nine kinds of thogai.",["There are six.","A word is hidden."]),
 ["m|How many kinds of thogainilai thodar?|Six|Nine|Three|Six.","m|In thogai nilai thodar|a word is hidden|nothing changes|a vowel is added|Hidden element.","t|Ummaith-thogai hides the word உம்.|T|Yes.","m|Simile hidden is|உவமைத்தொகை|வினைத்தொகை|பண்புத்தொகை|Uvamaith-thogai.","s|Which thogai hides a verb with tense?|வினைத்தொகை;vinaiththogai|Vinaiththogai.","t|You should first open out the hidden word.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"thirukkural-iyal3","Thirukkural (திருக்குறள்) — selected couplets, Iyal 3",
 "Valluvar says a guest is a treasure.",
 "Thirukkural is a book of 1330 two-line couplets in 133 chapters, by Thiruvalluvar. This unit's kurals are on hospitality and related virtues.",
 "The kurals teach that welcoming guests is a duty of a householder and a sign of a cultured life.",
 "Learn each kural with its word-by-word meaning. Revise the chapter name (அதிகாரம்) and the part (பால்).",
 ["குறள்","விருந்தோம்பல்","அதிகாரம்","பால்","வள்ளுவர்"],
 ("A householder need not welcome guests.",["It is a duty.","It shows culture."]),
 ["m|Thirukkural is by|Thiruvalluvar|Kamban|Ilango|Thiruvalluvar.","m|Total chapters|133|130|1330|133.","t|There are 1330 kurals.|T|Yes.","m|The theme here is|hospitality|war|travel|Virunthombal.","s|How many lines in a kural?|two;2|Two.","t|Welcoming guests is a duty.|T|Yes."])
I4="Iyal 4: Education (கல்வி)"
T(4,I4,"mozhipeyarppuk-kalvi","Mozhipeyarppuk Kalvi (மொழிபெயர்ப்புக் கல்வி)",
 "Translation opens the doors to other languages and to the world.",
 "This prose lesson by Manavai Mustafa explains that translation is essential for a language to grow and for connecting with the world. The Chinnamanur copper plates show that translation was done in Tamil even in Sangam times, and works were translated from Sanskrit and other languages.",
 "Translation brings knowledge from other languages into Tamil and carries Tamil to the world. It is also a field of education and employment.",
 "Terms: மொழிபெயர்ப்பு (translation), செப்பேடு (copper plate), மொழிவளம் (richness of a language) and கல்வி.",
 ["மொழிபெயர்ப்பு","செப்பேடு","மொழிவளம்","கல்வி","மணவை முஸ்தபா"],
 ("Translation is not needed.",["It helps languages grow.","It connects us to the world."]),
 ["m|மொழிபெயர்ப்பு means|translation|a poem|a dance|Translation.","m|The Chinnamanur plates show|translation in early times|farming|trade|Early translation.","t|Translation helps a language grow.|T|Yes.","m|செப்பேடு is a|copper plate|stone|palm leaf|Copper plate.","s|Who wrote this lesson?|Manavai Mustafa;மணவை முஸ்தபா|Manavai Mustafa.","t|Translation connects us to the world.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"thiruvilaiyadal-puranam","Thiruvilaiyadal Puranam (திருவிளையாடற் புராணம்)",
 "Sixty-four sports of Lord Shiva at Madurai in verse.",
 "Thiruvilaiyadal Puranam, composed by Paranjothi Munivar, narrates the sixty-four divine sports (திருவிளையாடல்கள்) of Lord Shiva at Madurai. The memorisation poem in the textbook is from this epic.",
 "The poems show devotion and rich storytelling about Madurai. Read the poem and learn its meaning.",
 "Terms: புராணம், திருவிளையாடல் (divine sport), மதுரை and பரஞ்சோதி முனிவர்.",
 ["திருவிளையாடல்","புராணம்","மதுரை","பரஞ்சோதிமுனிவர்","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("It describes thirty sports.",["It describes sixty-four.","It is set in Madurai."]),
 ["m|The author is|Paranjothi Munivar|Sekkizhar|Kamban|Paranjothi Munivar.","m|The sports are set in|Madurai|Chennai|Kasi|Madurai.","t|There are sixty-four sports.|T|Yes.","m|திருவிளையாடல் means|divine sport|war|book|Divine play.","s|What does புராணம் mean?|sacred story;purana|A sacred story.","t|The poem is memorised.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"puthiya-nambikkai","Puthiya Nambikkai (புதிய நம்பிக்கை) by Kamalalayan",
 "Some people walk where there is no path and make a highway for others.",
 "This prose lesson by Kamalalayan says that people come into history and some become history itself. They make a single-footed path where none existed and turn it into a highway. The lesson then speaks of how education changes lives.",
 "It encourages us to have new hope through education and effort. Even one person can open a way for many.",
 "Terms: நம்பிக்கை (hope), வரலாறு (history), பாதை (path) and கல்வி.",
 ["நம்பிக்கை","வரலாறு","பாதை","கல்வி","முயற்சி"],
 ("The lesson says effort is useless.",["Effort opens paths.","Hope grows through education."]),
 ["m|நம்பிக்கை means|hope|fear|anger|Hope.","m|The lesson is by|Kamalalayan|Kannadasan|Kalki|Kamalalayan.","t|Some people become history.|T|Yes.","m|பாதை means|path|river|hill|Path.","s|What does வரலாறு mean?|history|History.","t|Education brings new hope.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"ilakkanam-podhu","Grammar: General grammar review (இலக்கணம் - பொது)",
 "A quick revision of the main ideas of Tamil grammar.",
 "இலக்கணம் - பொது is a general grammar section that revises the five parts of Tamil grammar: எழுத்து, சொல், பொருள், யாப்பு and அணி. It helps you connect letters, words, meaning, verse and figures of speech.",
 "The section gives examples and exercises so that you can recall earlier lessons and apply them to reading and writing.",
 "Make a chart of the five parts with one example each, and revise earlier rules such as the types of words, sandhi and phrases.",
 ["இலக்கணம்","எழுத்து","சொல்","பொருள்","அணி"],
 ("Tamil grammar has three parts.",["It has five.","Letter, word, meaning, verse, figure."]),
 ["m|Number of parts of Tamil grammar|Five|Three|Two|Five.","m|யாப்பு is|prosody|letters|words|Prosody.","t|அணி means figure of speech.|T|Yes.","m|எழுத்து is|letters|verse|meaning|Letters.","s|What does இலக்கணம் mean?|grammar|Grammar.","t|The section revises earlier rules.|T|Yes."])
I5="Iyal 5: Arts, Beauty and Novelty (கலை, அழகியல், புதுமை)"
T(5,I5,"panmuga-kalaignar","Panmuga Kalaignar (பன்முகக் கலைஞர்)",
 "A person whose chosen name outshone his birth name.",
 "This prose lesson is about Kalaignar M. Karunanidhi, whose adopted name outlived his given name and in whom art took pride. It cites Professor Anbazhagan's view that he was a thinker who spread rational ideas, and presents him as a many-sided artist, a writer, orator, dramatist and film writer.",
 "It shows many faces of an artist and how art can serve society. It also encourages us to develop our own talents.",
 "Terms: பன்முகம் (many-sided), கலைஞர் (artist), எழுத்தாளர் (writer) and பேச்சாளர் (orator).",
 ["பன்முகம்","கலைஞர்","எழுத்தாளர்","பேச்சாளர்","திறமை"],
 ("He had only one talent.",["He had many.","He was a writer and orator."]),
 ["m|பன்முகம் means|many-sided|one-sided|silent|Many-sided.","m|The lesson is about|Kalaignar Karunanidhi|Kannadasan|Kamban|Kalaignar.","t|He was a writer and speaker.|T|Yes.","m|கலைஞர் means|artist|farmer|trader|Artist.","s|What does எழுத்தாளர் mean?|writer|Writer.","t|The lesson encourages developing talents.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"kambaramayanam","Kambaramayanam (கம்பராமாயணம்)",
 "The great Tamil Ramayana by Kamban.",
 "Kambaramayanam, composed by Kamban, is the Tamil retelling of the Ramayana and a high point of Tamil poetry. The textbook gives a memorisation poem from it.",
 "Kamban's verse is praised for its rich imagery, rhythm and depth. The poem shows his skill with description and character.",
 "Terms: கம்பர் (Kamban), இராமாயணம், காண்டம் (book) and மனப்பாடம். Learn the poem with its meaning.",
 ["கம்பர்","இராமாயணம்","காண்டம்","கவிச்சக்கரவர்த்தி","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("Kamban wrote the Silappadikaram.",["He wrote the Ramayana in Tamil.","He is a great poet."]),
 ["m|Kambaramayanam is by|Kamban|Ilango|Sekkizhar|Kamban.","m|It retells the|Ramayana|Mahabharata|Silappadikaram|Ramayana.","t|It is a high point of Tamil poetry.|T|Yes.","m|Kamban is called|Kavichakravarthy|Thiruvalluvar|Bharathi|Poet emperor.","s|Name the epic Kamban composed.|Ramayana;Kambaramayanam|Kambaramayanam.","t|The textbook poem is for memorisation.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"paaichal","Paaichal (பாய்ச்சல்) by Sa. Kandasamy",
 "A true artist is devoted to his art regardless of age or tiredness.",
 "Paaichal is a short story by Sa. Kandasamy. It says a real artist gives himself wholly to his art, stands apart from other artists with his own special qualities, and is not hampered by age or physical weariness.",
 "The story shows dedication and originality in art. It encourages us to follow our passion with full commitment.",
 "Terms: பாய்ச்சல் (a leap), கலைஞன், ஈடுபாடு (involvement) and தனித்தன்மை (uniqueness).",
 ["பாய்ச்சல்","கலைஞன்","ஈடுபாடு","தனித்தன்மை","சிறுகதை"],
 ("Age stops a true artist.",["It does not.","He is devoted."]),
 ["m|The story is by|Sa. Kandasamy|Kannadasan|Kambar|Sa. Kandasamy.","m|A true artist is|devoted to his art|lazy|afraid|Devoted.","t|He has his own special qualities.|T|Yes.","m|ஈடுபாடு means|involvement|travel|fear|Involvement.","s|What does தனித்தன்மை mean?|uniqueness|Uniqueness.","t|Age does not affect a true artist's devotion.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"agapporul-ilakkanam","Grammar: Love themes (அகப்பொருள் இலக்கணம்)",
 "Tamil poetry has a grammar for love and a grammar for war.",
 "அகப்பொருள் is the poetry of the inner life, that is, love, as laid down in grammar such as Tholkappiyam. It has the five landscapes (ஐந்திணை): குறிஞ்சி, முல்லை, மருதம், நெய்தல் and பாலை, plus கைக்கிளை and பெருந்திணை.",
 "Each landscape has a first object (முதற்பொருள்), a native object (கருப்பொருள்) and a feeling (உரிப்பொருள்). For example, குறிஞ்சி has union as its feeling and the mountain as its place.",
 "Memorise the five landscapes with their feelings: குறிஞ்சி - புணர்தல், முல்லை - இருத்தல், மருதம் - ஊடல், நெய்தல் - இரங்கல், பாலை - பிரிதல்.",
 ["அகப்பொருள்","ஐந்திணை","குறிஞ்சி","உரிப்பொருள்","கருப்பொருள்"],
 ("Agapporul is about war.",["It is about love.","Purapporul is about war."]),
 ["m|Agapporul is about|love|war|farming|Inner life.","m|Marutham's feeling is|ஊடல் (sulking)|பிரிதல்|இருத்தல்|Oodal.","t|There are five main landscapes.|T|Yes.","m|குறிஞ்சி is the|mountain|sea|desert|Hill.","s|What is the feeling of பாலை?|பிரிதல்;separation|Separation.","t|உரிப்பொருள் means the feeling.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"thirukkural-iyal5","Thirukkural (திருக்குறள்) — selected couplets, Iyal 5",
 "Brief verses on beauty, art and conduct.",
 "Thirukkural, by Thiruvalluvar, has 1330 couplets in three parts: aram, porul and inbam. The selection here goes with the theme of arts and beauty.",
 "Each kural has a precise meaning and is useful in everyday life.",
 "Learn the kural's words, meaning and chapter name; practise explaining it in your own words.",
 ["குறள்","அறம்","பொருள்","இன்பம்","வள்ளுவர்"],
 ("There are 130 chapters.",["There are 133.","Each has ten kurals."]),
 ["m|Kurals total|1330|1000|133|1330.","m|Author|Thiruvalluvar|Kamban|Bharathi|Valluvar.","t|It has three parts.|T|Yes.","m|Each kural has|two lines|four lines|eight lines|Two.","s|How many kurals per chapter?|ten;10|Ten.","t|Kurals help daily life.|T|Yes."])
I6="Iyal 6: Civilisation, Country and Society (நாகரிகம், நாடு, சமூகம்)"
T(6,I6,"sitragal-oli","Sitrakal Oli (சிற்றகல் ஒளி) by Ma. Po. Sivagnanam",
 "A small lamp can light up a great mind.",
 "This lesson by Ma. Po. Sivagnanam says that everyone loves to listen to stories from childhood; reading stories is the next step, and it makes one a reader and a creator. It then presents a writer who makes himself known through his writing.",
 "The lesson shows how reading and writing shape a person and how even a small light of learning can brighten a life.",
 "Terms: சிற்றகல் (small lamp), ஒளி (light), படைப்பாளி (creator) and வாசிப்பு (reading).",
 ["சிற்றகல்","ஒளி","படைப்பாளி","வாசிப்பு","கதை"],
 ("Stories have no value.",["They shape a reader.","They make a writer."]),
 ["m|சிற்றகல் means|small lamp|big sun|stone|Small lamp.","m|The lesson is by|Ma. Po. Sivagnanam|Kannadasan|Kamban|Ma. Po. Si.","t|Reading makes a person mature.|T|Yes.","m|படைப்பாளி means|creator|farmer|thief|A creator.","s|What does ஒளி mean?|light|Light.","t|The lesson begins with story-listening.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"silappathikaram","Silappathikaram (சிலப்பதிகாரம்)",
 "A tale of a anklet that shook a kingdom.",
 "Silappathikaram, composed by Ilango Adigal, is one of the five great Tamil epics and the story of Kovalan, Kannagi and Madhavi. It is divided into three kandams: Pugarkandam, Maduraikandam and Vanjikandam.",
 "The epic teaches that a ruler must be just and that chastity and justice are great virtues. Kannagi's anklet leads to the downfall of the Pandya king and the burning of Madurai.",
 "Terms: சிலம்பு (anklet), காண்டம் (section), இளங்கோவடிகள் and முத்தமிழ்க்காப்பியம். Learn the three kandams.",
 ["சிலப்பதிகாரம்","இளங்கோவடிகள்","கண்ணகி","கோவலன்","காண்டம்"],
 ("The epic was written by Kamban.",["Ilango Adigal wrote it.","It has three kandams."]),
 ["m|Silappathikaram was composed by|Ilango Adigal|Kamban|Sekkizhar|Ilango.","m|The heroine is|Kannagi|Manimegalai|Seetha|Kannagi.","t|It has three kandams.|T|Yes.","m|Which is a kandam?|Maduraikandam|Balakandam|Yuddhakandam|Madurai.","s|What does சிலம்பு mean?|anklet|Anklet.","t|It teaches that rulers must be just.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"mutholayiram","Muthollayiram (முத்தொள்ளாயிரம்)",
 "Short verses in praise of three great Tamil kings.",
 "Muthollayiram is an old Tamil poetic work, now available only in parts, in which each of the three crowned kings, Chera, Chola and Pandya, is praised in about nine hundred verses. The textbook gives a memorisation poem from it.",
 "The verses praise the valour and generosity of the kings and describe imaginative scenes.",
 "Terms: மூவேந்தர் (the three kings), சேரன், சோழன், பாண்டியன் and மனப்பாடம்.",
 ["முத்தொள்ளாயிரம்","மூவேந்தர்","சேரன்","சோழன்","பாண்டியன்"],
 ("It praises one king only.",["It praises three kings.","They are Chera, Chola and Pandya."]),
 ["m|It praises|the three Tamil kings|a god|a river|Muvendar.","m|The three kings are Chera, Chola and|Pandya|Pallava|Maurya|Pandya.","t|Only some verses survive.|T|Yes.","m|மூவேந்தர் means|three kings|three seas|three books|Three crowned kings.","s|Which king is called சோழன்?|Chola|Chola king.","t|It is a memorisation poem.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"vithai-nel-mangaiyaraai","Vithai Nel: Mangaiyaraai Pirappatharke (விதை நெல்: மங்கையராய்ப் பிறப்பதற்கே...)",
 "Women who excelled in many fields are like seed paddy for the future.",
 "This lesson begins by calling the world a wide ground where some dance, some sing and some show other skills; those who win are many, and this is personality. It then introduces women of strong personality.",
 "It presents women achievers and inspires girls to follow their talents.",
 "Terms: ஆளுமை (personality), மங்கை (woman), விதைநெல் (seed paddy) and சாதனை (achievement).",
 ["ஆளுமை","மங்கை","விதைநெல்","சாதனை","பெண்கள்"],
 ("The lesson is about men only.",["It is about women.","It speaks of achievement."]),
 ["m|ஆளுமை means|personality|poverty|weather|Personality.","m|The lesson is about|women achievers|farmers only|kings|Women.","t|The world is described as a wide ground.|T|Yes.","m|சாதனை means|achievement|failure|sleep|Achievement.","s|What does மங்கை mean?|woman|Woman.","t|It inspires girls.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"purapporul-ilakkanam","Grammar: War themes (புறப்பொருள் இலக்கணம்)",
 "Tamil poetry also has a grammar for war and public life.",
 "புறப்பொருள் is the poetry of outer life: war, valour, charity and governance. Each war stage has a flower, called a திணை, such as வெட்சி (cattle raiding), கரந்தை (cattle recovery), வஞ்சி (invasion), காஞ்சி (impermanence), நொச்சி (defence of the fort), உழிஞை (siege), தும்பை (battle) and வாகை (victory). Then comes பாடாண் (praise).",
 "Each form of poetry has a related stage of the war or a theme of public life. These correspond with the inner-life landscapes.",
 "Memorise the eight war themes in order and the flower of each; then recall an example poem from Purananuru.",
 ["புறப்பொருள்","வெட்சி","வஞ்சி","தும்பை","வாகை"],
 ("Purapporul is about love.",["It is about outer life.","Agapporul is love."]),
 ["m|Thumbai is the|battle|siege|victory|Battle theme.","m|Vaagai is|victory|raiding|siege|Victory.","t|Vanji is invasion.|T|Yes.","m|பாடாண் means|praise poems|a siege|a lament|Praising a hero.","s|What is the grammar of outer life called?|புறப்பொருள்;purapporul|Purapporul.","t|Each war stage has a flower.|T|Yes."])
I7="Iyal 7: Virtue, Philosophy and Thought (அறம், தத்துவம், சிந்தனை)"
T(7,I7,"sanga-ilakkiyaththil-aram","Sanga Ilakkiyaththil Aram (சங்க இலக்கியத்தில் அறம்)",
 "The Sangam Tamils earned wealth to do good.",
 "This prose lesson says that Tamils earned wealth and enjoyed doing good, took household life as a life of virtue, and refused acts that would bring blame even if the whole world were the reward. In Sangam times virtue was the centre of human relations, free of religious mixture.",
 "The lesson shows that virtue (அறம்) was seen as a social value that includes charity, truth and justice.",
 "Terms: அறம் (virtue), சங்க இலக்கியம், இல்வாழ்க்கை (household life) and பழி (blame).",
 ["அறம்","சங்க இலக்கியம்","இல்வாழ்க்கை","பழி","ஈகை"],
 ("Sangam Tamils ignored virtue.",["They held virtue central.","They avoided blame."]),
 ["m|அறம் means|virtue|war|trade|Virtue.","m|Sangam Tamils took household life as a life of|virtue|war|travel|Aram.","t|They refused blameworthy acts.|T|Yes.","m|பழி means|blame|praise|gift|Blame.","s|What does இல்வாழ்க்கை mean?|household life;family life|Domestic life.","t|Virtue was central to human relations.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"thembavani","Thembavani (தேம்பாவணி) by Veeramamunivar",
 "An Italian missionary writes a Tamil epic.",
 "Thembavani, composed by Constantius Beschi, known in Tamil as Veeramamunivar, is a Tamil epic on the life of St Joseph. Its name means a garland of unfading honey-sweet verses. The textbook includes a memorisation poem from it.",
 "It shows that Tamil literature has been enriched by people of many cultures and religions.",
 "Terms: தேம்பாவணி (unfading garland), வீரமாமுனிவர், காப்பியம் and மனப்பாடம்.",
 ["தேம்பாவணி","வீரமாமுனிவர்","காப்பியம்","புனித யோசேப்பு","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("Thembavani was written by Kamban.",["It was written by Veeramamunivar.","It is a Tamil epic."]),
 ["m|Thembavani is by|Veeramamunivar|Kamban|Ilango|Veeramamunivar.","m|It tells the life of|St Joseph|Rama|Kovalan|St Joseph.","t|It is a Tamil epic.|T|Yes.","m|தேம்பாவணி means|unfading garland|golden bowl|silver bell|The garland.","s|What is the author's Tamil name?|வீரமாமுனிவர்;Veeramamunivar|Veeramamunivar.","t|The author came from Italy.|T|Beschi was Italian."])
T(7,I7,"akkarai","Akkarai (அக்கறை) by Kalyanji",
 "Small happenings may hide great human feeling.",
 "Akkarai is a new poem by Kalyanji. New poetry finds paths for living in everyday events: many small events catch our eye but do not reach our heart. The poet picks such neglected, human moments.",
 "The poem invites us to care (அக்கறை) about people and small things around us.",
 "Terms: அக்கறை (concern or care), புதுக்கவிதை, மனிதநேயம் (humanity) and அன்றாடம் (daily).",
 ["அக்கறை","புதுக்கவிதை","மனிதநேயம்","அன்றாடம்","கவிதை"],
 ("The poem is about royal wars.",["It is about everyday life.","It teaches care."]),
 ["m|அக்கறை means|care|anger|speed|Concern.","m|The poem is|free verse|an epic|a play|Puthukkavithai.","t|It finds meaning in small events.|T|Yes.","m|மனிதநேயம் means|humanity|geography|sleep|Humaneness.","s|Who wrote Akkarai?|Kalyanji;கல்யாண்ஜி|Kalyanji.","t|The poem invites care for others.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"peruvazhi-ramanujar","Peruvazhi: Ramanujar (பெருவழி: இராமானுசர்) — play",
 "A great teacher who opened the temple of knowledge to all.",
 "Peruvazhi is a drama in the textbook about Ramanujar, a saint who taught equality and brotherhood. A drama tells its story through dialogue and action, so read it with attention to the characters.",
 "The play brings out the message of equality and compassion in religion. Read the play in your textbook for its scenes and lines.",
 "Terms: நாடகம் (drama), உரையாடல் (dialogue), இராமானுசர் and சமத்துவம் (equality).",
 ["நாடகம்","உரையாடல்","இராமானுசர்","சமத்துவம்","அன்பு"],
 ("The lesson is a poem.",["It is a drama.","It stresses equality."]),
 ["m|Peruvazhi is a|drama|poem|dictionary|Play.","m|The play is about|Ramanujar|Kamban|Valluvar|Ramanuja.","t|It stresses equality.|T|Yes.","m|உரையாடல் means|dialogue|map|song|Dialogue.","s|What does நாடகம் mean?|drama|Drama.","t|The play has characters and dialogue.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"pa-vagai-alagidudhal","Grammar: Types of verse and scansion (பா வகை, அலகிடுதல்)",
 "Poems have a hidden pattern that you can count.",
 "Tamil verse (பா) has four main types: வெண்பா, ஆசிரியப்பா, கலிப்பா and வஞ்சிப்பா. Each has its own seer pattern and line count. அலகிடுதல் means scanning a line by dividing it into அசை and சீர்.",
 "To scan, mark each syllable as நேர் or நிரை, group them into சீர்கள், and name the foot (e.g. தேமா, புளிமா). Thirukkural is in kural venba, a short form of venba.",
 "Practise scanning two-line kurals and four-line venbas, and note the ending of each type.",
 ["பா","வெண்பா","ஆசிரியப்பா","அலகிடுதல்","சீர்"],
 ("There are only two verse types.",["There are four.","Venba, asiriyappa, kali, vanji."]),
 ["m|Number of main verse types|Four|Two|Eight|Four.","m|Scansion is called|அலகிடுதல்|பொருள்கோள்|அணி|Alakidudhal.","t|Thirukkural is in kural venba.|T|Yes.","m|Venba is|a verse type|a word|a poet|Verse type.","s|What does சீர் mean?|foot;metrical foot|Metrical foot.","t|Scanning divides a line into asai.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"thirukkural-iyal7","Thirukkural (திருக்குறள்) — selected couplets, Iyal 7",
 "Thiruvalluvar guides us on virtue, thought and life.",
 "The last selection of kurals gives guidance on virtue and wise living. Thirukkural has 1330 couplets in 133 chapters.",
 "The couplets are short and universal, and each can guide a decision in life. Learn them with their meanings.",
 "Revise all selected kurals with their chapter names and meanings, and practise writing each in your own words.",
 ["குறள்","அறம்","அதிகாரம்","வள்ளுவர்","வாழ்க்கை"],
 ("Thirukkural is only about farming.",["It speaks of virtue, wealth and love.","It guides life."]),
 ["m|Total kurals|1330|133|1000|1330.","m|Author|Thiruvalluvar|Kamban|Ilango|Valluvar.","t|Each chapter has ten kurals.|T|Yes.","m|Parts|three|two|five|Three.","s|How many chapters?|133;133 chapters|133.","t|The kurals are universal.|T|Yes."])
